messages.content:
{
 "what_you_observe": [
  "Tuesday, February 2. Seven pm.",
  "Phil rides the coach and steps off at Pittsburgh.",
  "Rita said in the lobby: I don't speak to the crew. I push the door and go.",
  "Larry said in the lobby: To the crew, over my shoulder, not turning around: \"Taking the charge. Alma's got a girl in Pittsburgh and the place is going dark. You guys shoot the ballroom tonight, I'll be back.\"",
  "You are now at Pittsburgh.",
  "There is time for one evening visit. The ballroom lights are on and the station line is open."
 ],
 "your_own_memories": [
  {
   "when": "last Tuesday afternoon",
   "witnessed": "Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh.."
  },
  {
   "when": "last evening in Pittsburgh",
   "witnessed": "You reached your sister from the terminal payphone. She confirmed the van booking for Wednesday.",
   "your_words": "Hi, is the van driver still confirming for 8 AM tomorrow? I'm at the terminal now."
  },
  {
   "when": "this morning",
   "witnessed": "After that evening in Pittsburgh you woke back in your hotel bed. The radio again announced Tuesday, February 2."
  },
  {
   "what_you_did": "Phil rides the coach and steps off at Pittsburgh.",
   "what_you_said": "\"Coach is at nine. I've got a couch in Pittsburgh on Wednesday. Be seeing you.\"",
   "your_intention": "Be in Pittsburgh on that coach. Be at my sister's door before eight on Wednesday. Couch goes through the door, not the window. I don't need a piano lesson or a reel of film or a flat tire fixed to do this. I need to be on a moving vehicle for roughly four hours and then I need to be where the couch is. That's the whole plan. That's the whole day. The radio will still say Tuesday when I wake up and I'll still be in the hotel and I'll still be doing this. Fine. I'll do it. I'll do it until the couch is on the other side of the hallway and my sister isn't looking at me like I'm a broken promise. The ticket is paid. The seat is there. I sit in it."
  },
  "Phil rides the coach and steps off at Pittsburgh.",
  "Rita said in the lobby: I don't speak to the crew. I push the door and go.",
  "Larry said in the lobby: To the crew, over my shoulder, not turning around: \"Taking the charge. Alma's got a girl in Pittsburgh and the place is going dark. You guys shoot the ballroom tonight, I'll be back.\"",
  "You are now at Pittsburgh."
 ],
 "who_you_are_with": "your present location",
 "physical_choices": {
  "call_sister": "Use the Pittsburgh payphone to call your sister.",
  "sleep_at_terminal": "Sleep on the terminal bench.",
  "wait_for_morning": "Sit up through the evening and wait for morning."
 }
}

{
  "action": "call_sister",
  "detail": "I walk to the payphone. The one with the sticky coin slot and the little placard that says CALLS TO BE MADE IN A MANNER APPROPRIATE TO THE TERMINAL. I don't care about the placard. I put the quarter in. I dial. I know the number. I've dialed it before. The ring is long. One. Two. Three. Four. Five. Six. Seven. Eight. Then the click and her voice, flat and tired, the way she sounds when the kitchen is a mess and the couch is still blocking the hallway and she's already made herself a cup of tea and she's not optimistic about the evening.",
  "intention": "Remove the last variable. She should not be sitting in that kitchen on Wednesday morning, listening for the van, wondering if her brother made the four-hour ride or if he's still in the hotel or if the coach was full or if he just... didn't come. I am in the city. I am not going back to the hotel. I am going to sleep on this bench and I am going to be at her door at seven-thirty and the couch is going to go through the door and I don't need anyone to believe me, I just need her to know where I am and when I'm coming and that the van is still at eight and I'm not going to make her call the driver to confirm again. That's the whole call. I'm not explaining the loop. I'm not explaining the Tuesday that won't end. I'm not explaining why I'm calling from a payphone in a city I'm supposed to be in tomorrow. I'm telling her where I am. I'm telling her the time I'll be at the door. I'm telling her the couch is going to move. Then I hang up. Then I sit on the bench. The wood is cold through my coat. The terminal is quiet. The coach is at the far end of the platform and the driver is already in the cab and the lights are on and I don't get back on it. I don't get back on it. I stay here. I stay here and in the morning the radio will say Tuesday and I will be in Pittsburgh and I will walk to my sister's door and the couch will be on the other side of the hallway and she will not be looking at me like I'm a broken promise. The ticket is paid. The seat was there. I sat in it. I'm here. I'm not going back.",
  "words": "\"Hi. It's Phil. I'm in Pittsburgh. I'm not going back to the hotel tonight. I'll be at your door at seven-thirty. The van's still at eight. I'm not calling the driver. I'm not calling you again. I'm at the door at seven-thirty. Okay. Okay. Good night. I'll see you in the morning.\""
}
